## Current roadmap / platform inheritance

GitHub #78 and `docs/MESSENGER_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE.md` are the current product/platform authority. Vimla is messenger-first with one backend for Web and future Desktop/Mobile. This rule's domain-specific constraints remain valid and must not be interpreted using the old workspace-first phase order.

Component reuse in this rule means current Web/Admin DOM reuse and later Web/Desktop reuse after #123. Do not force React Native Mobile to consume DOM components solely for reuse metrics; share logic/tokens/contracts instead.



# Canonical component reuse

Before creating UI, search `@vimla/ui`. Reuse first, extend second, create page-local only for genuinely unique domain composition.

Never create page-local substitutes for shared buttons, inputs, select, tabs, segmented controls, switches, checkboxes, menu/dropdown, dialog/sheet, toast/alert, list rows, navigation, composer or model selector.

If multiple pages need a new visual pattern, it belongs in `@vimla/ui`.
